16 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Three-panel photograph of a blooming orchard shows rows of soil and young trees with branches bearing clusters of small pink and white blossoms, fresh green leaves, and scattered ground vegetation under clear daylight.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Flowchart with color-coded horizontal sections details an image acquisition protocol for orchard study: Pre-acquisition setup includes location, date, and device specifications; multi-strategy acquisition covers spatial coverage, viewpoint diversity, scale, lighting, and natural flower conditions; field execution addresses personnel and constraints; post-processing involves image review and metadata recording.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Panel a shows a branch with clusters of light pink and white apple blossoms and several pink buds surrounded by green leaves. Panel b displays a similar branch with numerous buds and a few open blossoms, highlighting the varying stages of blooming. Panel c features a dense cluster of apple blossoms with mostly open pale flowers and some remaining pink buds, shown near the trunk and branches.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating an annotation workflow: strategy establishment with guidelines for labeling flowers and buds, single-annotator training and annotation, expert review for class and positional accuracy, and final verification with checkmark icons representing each stage.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Screenshot of a labeling software interface displaying an image of apple blossoms and buds on a tree branch, with two red boxes indicating excluded instances. Green keypoints and blue bounding boxes mark flower and bud locations, and a list of labeled categories appears on the right.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Panel \(a\) shows a histogram with a normal curve overlay depicting the log-scale size distribution of box areas in pixels squared, with counts peaking near the center. Panel \(b\) presents a spatial heatmap with intensity from black to yellow representing higher concentrations, indicating spatial density centered in the image area. Panel \(c\) provides a grouped boxplot comparison of box area between Bud and Apple flower classes, showing Buds generally have larger median areas, with visible outliers.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Six-panel grouped photograph labeled a to f showing apple tree branches with white blossoms under different lighting conditions. Panels a and b are brightly lit, c is an upside-down version, d and e are progressively darker, and f is both dark and upside-down.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Panel a shows a close-up of a cluster of white and pale pink apple blossoms on a tree branch surrounded by green leaves. Panel b displays a branch with green leaves and numerous unopened red flower buds. Panel c presents a branch with both white and pink apple blossoms, along with several unopened buds and green leaves, positioned near a wooden support.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Twelve-panel grid of training metrics for three models: YOLO11n, RT-DETR-L, and DEIMv2-N, showing line graphs for train loss, validation loss, mAP50, and mAP50-95 across one hundred epochs. DEIMv2-N has \215Not Applicable\216 indicated for validation loss. All loss values decrease over time, while mAP metrics increase, indicating model improvement during training. Each model\220s data is color-coded: YOLO11n in blue, RT-DETR-L in red, and DEIMv2-N in green.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
